<title>USA: U.S. NAPM index 52.6 in Aug versus 50.2 in July.</title>
<headline>U.S. NAPM index 52.6 in Aug versus 50.2 in July.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) said on Tuesday its index of maufacturing activity rose to 52.6 in August from 50.2 in July. A listing of the main NAPM components follows:</p>
<p>		    Aug   July  June  May  April  March  Feb   Jan</p>
<p>PMI		 52.6  50.2  54.3  49.3  50.1  46.9  45.2  44.2</p>
<p>Production	57.0  52.4  55.4  52.7  52.1  46.6  44.0  44.4</p>
<p>New Orders	55.6  54.0  61.3  52.4  53.8  49.7  44.7  41.6</p>
<p>Supplier Deliv  52.5  50.9  53.2  50.0  49.2  49.9  50.1  46.9 Inventories     41.6  41.2  42.3  38.3  44.6  38.8  43.9  47.7</p>
<p>Employment	48.2  45.5  49.4  45.5  45.3  44.7  44.3  44.3</p>
<p>Prices	    47.4  44.5  49.0  50.8  40.1  39.5  38.3  39.4</p>
<p>Export Orders   57.2  53.8  53.9  56.9  51.4  50.4  49.4  49.3</p>
<p>Imports	   50.6  53.7  48.6  49.8  46.2  46.3  47.6  48.0</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
